architect › Spec is clear, project is `bun test`, `src/wrap.ts` is a stub. Plan:

**`src/wrap.ts`** — implement `wrap(text, width)`:
1. `if (width < 1) throw new RangeError(...)` first.
2. Split the input into paragraphs on blank lines: `text.split(/\n\s*\n/)` (consumes runs of blank lines as one separator).
3. Per paragraph, tokenize with `para.trim().split(/\s+/)` — this collapses runs of spaces (and tabs) into one and drops leading/trailing whitespace; filter out empty tokens.
4. Greedy fill, emitting lines of at most `width` chars:
   - If a token is longer than `width`, break it into `width`-sized chunks first (so it flows across lines) and treat the chunks as ordinary tokens.
   - Append token to current line if the line is empty, or `line.length + 1 + token.length <= width`; otherwise flush the line and start a new one.
   - Joining words with a single `" "` satisfies "no line ends in a space" — never pad, never emit trailing spaces.
5. A paragraph whose token list is empty contributes one empty line (this is what keeps a blank line between paragraphs when joining).
6. Join each paragraph's lines with `"\n"`, join paragraphs with `"\n\n"`.

**`src/wrap.test.ts`** (new, bun:test) covering at least:
- fits on one line: `wrap("Hello world", 11)` → `"Hello world"`
- breaks at space: `wrap("Hello world", 5)` → `"Hello\nworld"`
- greedy packing: `wrap("The quick brown fox", 10)` → `"The quick\nbrown fox"`
- runs of spaces count as one, no trailing space: `wrap("Hello  world", 6)` → `"Hello\nworld"`
- word longer than width split: `wrap("abcdefghij", 3)` → `"abc\ndef\nghi\nj"`
- long word mixed with short: `wrap("x abcdefgh", 3)` → `"x\nabc\ndef\ngh"`
- paragraphs: `wrap("one two\n\nthree four", 10)` → `"one two\n\nthree four"`; also multiple consecutive blank lines collapse to one; blank-line round-trip with narrow width: `wrap("aaa bbb\n\nccc", 3)` → `"aaa\nbbb\n\nccc"`
- empty-ish input: `wrap("", 5)` → `""`
- `wrap("x", 0)` and `wrap("x", -1)` throw `RangeError` (`expect(() => ...).toThrow(RangeError)`)

**Check:** `bun test` — all tests pass (print the summary line). Commit the two files.
